+{
+  "task_id": "T14",
+  "repository": "aider",
+  "mode": "contract",
+  "evidence": [
+    {
+      "path": "aider/coders/search_replace.py",
+      "symbol": "search_and_replace",
+      "start_line": 434,
+      "end_line": 445,
+      "observation": "The exact-match edit engine: it counts occurrences of search_text in original_text (line 437) and, when the count is non-zero, returns original_text.replace(search_text, replace_text). Because the guard `# if num > 1: raise SearchTextNotUnique()` is commented out at lines 438-439, a unique search text is applied exactly once, a search text that appears twice would be rewritten at every occurrence, and a search text that appears zero times makes the function return None so nothing is mutated. This is the primitive the T14 contract pins down: exact (byte-for-byte, whitespace/newline-significant) matching, and the fact that uniqueness must be enforced by the caller."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/coders/search_replace.py",
+      "symbol": "SearchTextNotUnique",
+      "start_line": 524,
+      "end_line": 525,
+      "observation": "The designated failure signal for an ambiguous edit: a ValueError subclass exported from this module and imported by aider/coders/udiff_coder.py (line 8). It is the contract's distinction between 'edit failed cleanly' (raise / falsy result, file untouched) and 'edit silently applied to several places' (multi-occurrence str.replace). The demo asserts it stays a ValueError subclass so callers can keep translating it into the UnifiedDiffNotUnique error message."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/coders/search_replace.py",
+      "symbol": "flexible_search_and_replace",
+      "start_line": 565,
+      "end_line": 577,
+      "observation": "Dispatcher over (strategy, preproc) pairs that returns the first truthy result, i.e. the exact-match search_and_replace strategy is always attempted first (see editblock_strategies/udiff_strategies at lines 547-563 and the caller udiff_coder.flexi_just_search_and_replace at lines 201-206, which uses only (search_and_replace, all_preprocs)). Consequently a unique, byte-exact match is resolved once by search_and_replace without ever reaching the fuzzy diff-match-patch strategies, and a non-matching attempt returns None so the caller's refusal path stays clean."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/coders/search_replace.py",
+      "symbol": "strip_blank_lines",
+      "start_line": 611,
+      "end_line": 614,
+      "observation": "Whitespace/newline normalisation used by the preproc tuples in all_preprocs (lines 528-538) and applied by try_strategy (lines 586-608). It only trims leading/trailing blank lines of the three texts, so interior whitespace - such as the trailing spaces that make the T14 fixture's two blocks distinct - remains significant, and a whitespace-blind search text still fails to match. This is why the fixture's exact edit succeeds exactly once instead of being normalised onto the near-twin block."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/coders/udiff_coder.py",
+      "symbol": "directly_apply_hunk",
